sample-record-prose : List Word
sample-record-prose = "**1. The record.** A participant i is part of the universe's process (states X, histories h : ℕ → X) and receives it only through its observation o_i : X → Y_i. Its record to t is what it has received: R_i(t) = (o_i(h(t′)))_{t′<t}. Its state at t is a function of its record; that is tautological for a physical system, since nothing reaches i but through o_i. **2. Occurrences and identification.** An occurrence of a word w is an event of i's record R_i that i identifies as w. Identification is i's act on its record, since no two sound waves are equal. So for i a word is a type Occ_i(w): its points are events of the record, its paths are i's identifications of them. Every occurrence e has a context c(e) ∈ C, the record around it, which is itself made of occurrences and percepts and so carries the same structure one level up."
